*****************************************************************			   **              Copyright (C) 1989-1992		   **              All Rights Reserved		   **              Apple Computer, Inc.		   **			   *****************************************************************	title 'Menu Mgr Patch        GS ROM 3 Patch'********************************************************************	Menu manager patches for ROM 3** System Disk 5.0** 5/16/89	Everyone** Patch to PopUpMenuSelect to fix two bugs.  First, there* is a problem with the code that restores behind a popup* if the popup falls off the screen.  It restores too much.** Second, there was a field that was not initialized and the* first rectangle drawn could be drawn in the wrong place.** 19 May 89	Steven Glass** HiliteMenu did not work if the input was 0 or FFFF, we now* special case these and clean the stack instead of crashing.** 23 May 89	Yee** Take out patch to HiliteMenu because some applications * actually create menus with an ID of zero (which by the * way is not legal, i.e. of app is BounceIt)** 25 May 89	Mensch and Yee (thanks for including me in the journey)** Patched out a shit load of calls to fix the problem where* the handle to menu caches were being orphaned.* For all the calls that call the routines freeCache and* everycachefree we patch those calls out. In the patch we save * all the caches to each menu and then make sure we return back to * the patch so we can compare each saved cache to the cache currently * in each menu if they differ then that handle is disposed of.** 31 May 89	Mensch and Yee* * Make menu manager patch scrambler proof. We were not dereferencing* the menu bar handle before using it. (Change made in SaveAllCache,* we deref right before calling GetMFirst)** Take prototype bit out of version number. Final version = 3.1 for* System Disk 5.0.** 07 Sep 89	Yee** Patch NewMenuBar2. When the menubar is a resource, the resource* is not getting released properly. If the high word of the resource* ID is non-zero then we crash. If the high word is zero then the * resource just doesn't get released. This has been fixed.** 08 Mar 90	Yee** Install patch for icon support. You can now have icons in menu items.* Added the calls SetItemIcon and GetItemIcon. ** 13 Mar 90 ** Added the following calls: SetItemStruct($490F), GetItemStruct($4A0F),* RemoveItemStruct($4B0F), GetItemFlag2($4C0F), and SetItemFlag2($4D0F).** Patched the following existing calls: SetMItem, GetMItem, SetMItemName,* SetMItemName2, and CalcMenuSize.** 21 Mar 90	Yee* Fix bug in CalcMenuSize. Worksheet #MTLRAF013. I was referencing <itemptr* when it hadn't been setup yet.** 29 Mar 90	Yee* Fix bug in DeleteMenu. The handle of the menu getting removed from * the menu list was not getting unlocked.** 05 Apr 90	Yee* Change the way the menu item icons are drawn. I now use DrawIcon instead* of PPToPort to draw the icon. To use icons in menu items, the menu mgr* now requires that QDAux be started. Also the icon structure use to look* like a locInfo record, its now an icon structure as defined by rIcon.** 17-Sep-90	Dave Lyons** Changed e16.resource to e16.resources.  Removed all.macros.* Version is $8303.** 19-Sep-90	Dave Lyons** Added GetMItemBlink call.* Added code to MenuSelect patch to call InitCursor if the G_INITCURSOR* bit is set in the Menu Global flags and the cursor doesn't seem to* already be the arrow cursor.** 22-Oct-90	Dave Lyons** Patched EnableMItem and DisableMItem to return error $0001 if the* Menu Manager isn't started up yet (for compatibility with a stupid* third-party application).** 10-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Adding InsertPathMItems call (see Menu Manager source).** 17-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Patched PopUpMenuSelect to disable fastPorting, because the ROM* Menu Mgr is stuffing a bunch of values into the grafPort & not* letting QD know about it.  This was making items not always* hilite properly in pop-ups, at least when the items had icons.** 17-Feb-91	Dave Lyons** Postpatched MenuStartUp to set item blink from BRAM $5E, bits 3-4.** 3-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Patched MenuKey to call SendRequest($0F01) if no menu item is found* matching the key.** 14-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** If the MenuKey SendRequest call succeeds, now I change the event* into a null event so the caller doesn't try to handle it further.** 15-May-91	Dave Lyons** Fix InsertMenu to return dupMenuID on a duplicate menu ID being* inserted.** 21-May-91	Dave Lyons** Mask off high byte of the SetPurge parameter for a pop-up.* SetPurge was returning an error, since bit 31 is a flag here.** 22-May-91	Dave Lyons** Added a PHA I left out yesterday ("dumbshit move" sez Greg).** 25-Jul-91	Dave Lyons** Added restrictions to SendRequest($0F01=systemSaysMenuKey): Desk Manager must* be active, CDA-events must be postable (for Installer when it disables use* of DAs), and we must be dealing with the system menu bar.** 2-Aug-91	Dave Lyons** Fix above code--direct page wasn't set in this context (code was pasted in* from TOOL015).** 26-Aug-91	Dave Lyons** HideMenuBar now messes only with SCBs 2 through 9, instead of setting them all* to the MasterSCB.** SendRequest(systemSaysMenuKey) now has stop-after-one flag set.** 18-Sep-91	Dave Lyons** Made HideMenuBar mess with SCBs 0..MenuBarHeight-1, instead of just 2..9.* This is for HyperCard IIgs compatibility.** ??-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** Cleaned up some comments & dead text.** 8-Feb-92	Dave Lyons** Pre-patch MenuSelect to not pull down a menu so close to the* bottom of the screen that we trash stuff past the end of screen* memory.** Patch PopUpMenuSelect so it correctly gives the mGetItemID* message to custom pop-ups.** Version $0303 for 6.0.********************************************************************* 13-Mar-92	Dave Lyons** Version $8304 for 6.0.1.** 2-Apr-93 DAL** Version $0304 for 6.0.1.*******************************************************************	Blanks off	String asis		include 'all.macros'	;16-Jan-91 DAL	include 'e16.resources'	include 'e16.qdaux'	include ':::MenuMgr:MenuEquates.asm'	import FinishSetForeColor	import FinishPtInRectdispCtl	EQU $0004	; DefProc - Dispose	command.ToStrip	equ $E10184	; Jmp vector to 0ErrOut routineUnlockMenuBar	equ $FD62C4LockMenuHand	equ $FD62F1UnlockMenuHand	equ $FD6303DerefMenuHand	equ $FD6315LockMenuBar	equ $FD628BCache	equ $FD7D33MakeCache	equ $FD802FAllocateCache	equ $FD8052FreeCache	equ $FD80CFDoWhiteSpace	equ $FD69D9JustifyRight	equ $FD6F0DJustifyLeft	equ $FD6EFBAdjustBottom	equ $FD6B5FAdjustTop	equ $FD6B12AdjustRect	equ $FD6BAAGetIFirst	equ $FD7425Next_Item	equ $FD7437Dispatch	equ $FD6FC5InitStuff	equ $FD6A61GetColor	equ $FD6376SaveColor	equ $FD6A46GetMFirst	equ $FD6235Next_Menu	equ $FD6887FixTextFace	equ $FD8104PrintStrg	equ $FD7D1ELoadnRelease	equ $FD5BC4GetItemH	equ $FD740DIntoSizeMenu	equ $FD711Cto_uport	equ $FD635Cto_myport	equ $FD6327getmptr	equ $FD6238hline	equ $FD7446calcitem	equ $FD73ADinside	equ $FD6CBDgetiptr	equ $FD79BFbadCache	equ $FD8092parse_strg	equ $FD5CB4growBlock	equ $FD7714BackIntoRomSucker	equ $FD6DECPopEmptyInROM	equ $FD69B1RightAfterPullDown2Call equ $FD6988TheRTL	equ $FD577BROMMenuNewres	equ $FD57EBROMInsertMenu	equ $FD75E2ROMSetMTitleStart	equ $FD781AROMSetMTitleWidth	equ $FD7883ROMSetMenuTitle	equ $FD795DROMSetMenuTitle2	equ $FD7901ROMCalcMenuSize	equ $FD74E6ROMInsertMItem	equ $FD7564ROMInsertMItem2	equ $FD753AROMDeleteMItem	equ $FD764FROMDeleteMenu	equ $FD76D7;;;ROMMenuSelect	equ $FD6BBFpop0Bytes	equ $FD8FA3pop2Bytes	equ $FD8FABpop4Bytes	equ $FD8FB3pop6Bytes	equ $FD8FBBpop8Bytes	equ $FD8FC3popABytes	equ $FD8FCBepop2bytes	equ $FD8FAEepop8bytes	equ $FD8FC6	MACRO&lab	ROMCALL &where&lab	phk	pea @1-1	pea |TheRTL-1	jml &where@1	MEND;===========================================================================;          Menu Manager function table.;===========================================================================MenuCallTable	PROC EXPORT	import PopupMenuSelect	import MenuVersion	import MenuSelect	import HiliteMenu	import MenuNewRes	import InsertMenu	import SetMTitleStart	import SetMTitleWidth	import SetMenuTitle2	import SetMenuTitle	Import CalcMenuSize	import InsertMItem	import InsertMItem2	import deleteMItem	import DeleteMenu	import MenuStartUp	import MenuShutDown	import GetPopupDefProc	import NewMenuBar2	import SetItemIcon	import GetItemIcon	import SetItemStruct	import GetItemStruct	import RemoveItemStruct	import GetItemFlag2	import SetItemFlag2	import SetMItem	import GetItem	import SetMItemName	import SetMItemName2	import SetMItem2	import GetItemWidth	import GetMItemBlink	import EnableMItem	import DisableMItem	import InsertPathMItems	;10-Jan-91 DAL	import MenuKey		;3-Mar-91 DAL	import HideMenuBar		;26-Aug-91 DAL	ENTRY FPTFPT	DC.L (ENDFPT-FPT)/4	DC.L 0	 ;  MenuBootInit	$010F	DC.L MenuStartUp-1	 ;  MenuStartUp	$020F	DC.L MenuShutDown-1	 ;  MenuShutDown	$030F	DC.L MenuVersion-1	 ;	$040F	DC.L 0	 ;  MenuReset	$050F	DC.L 0	 ;  MenuStatus	$060F	DC.L 0	 ;  Reserved	$070F	DC.L 0	 ;  Reserved	$080F	DC.L MenuKey-1	;	$090F patched 3-Mar-91 DAL	DC.L 0	 ;  GetMenuBar	$0A0F	DC.L 0	 ;  MenuRefresh	$0B0F	DC.L 0	 ;  FlashMenuBar	$0C0F	DC.L InsertMenu-1	 ;  InsertMenu	$0D0F	DC.L DeleteMenu-1	 ;  DeleteMenu	$0E0F	DC.L InsertMItem-1	 ;  InsertMItem	$0F0F	DC.L DeleteMItem-1	 ;  DeleteMItem	$100F	DC.L 0	 ;  GetSysBar	$110F	DC.L 0	 ;  SetSysBar	$120F	DC.L 0	 ;  FixMenuBar	$130F	DC.L 0	 ;  CountMItems	$140F	DC.L 0	 ;  NewMenuBar	$150F	DC.L 0	 ;  GetMHandle	$160F	DC.L 0	 ;  SetBarColors	$170F	DC.L 0	 ;  GetBarColors	$180F	DC.L SetMTitleStart-1  ;  	$190F	DC.L 0	 ;  GetMTitleStart 	$1A0F	DC.L 0	 ;  GetMenuMgrPort 	$1B0F	DC.L CalcMenuSize-1	 ;  CalcMenuSize	$1C0F	DC.L SetMTitleWidth-1 	$1D0F	DC.L 0	 ;  GetMTitleWidth 	$1E0F	DC.L 0	 ;  SetMenuFlag	$1F0F	DC.L 0	 ;  GetMenuFlag	$200F	DC.L SetMenuTitle-1	 ;  SetMenuTitle	$210F	DC.L 0	 ;  GetMenuTitle	$220F	DC.L 0	 ;  MenuGlobal	$230F     Added 2/18/87	DC.L SetMItem-1		$240F	DC.L GetItem-1		$250F	DC.L 0	 ;  SetMItemFlag	$260F	DC.L 0	 ;  GetItemFlag	$270F	DC.L 0	 ;  SetItemBlink	$280F	DC.L MenuNewRes-1	 ;  MenuNewRes	$290F	DC.L 0	 ;  DrawMenuBar	$2A0F	DC.L MenuSelect-1	 ;  MenuSelect	$2B0F	DC.L 0	 ;  HiliteMenu      $2C0F	DC.L 0	 ;  NewMenu	$2D0F	DC.L 0	 ;  DisposeMenu	$2E0F	DC.L 0	 ;  InitPalette	$2F0F	DC.L EnableMItem-1	 ;	$300F patched 22-Oct-90 DAL	DC.L DisableMItem-1	 ;	$310F patched 22-Oct-90 DAL	DC.L 0	 ;  CheckMItem	$320F	DC.L 0	 ;  SetMItemMark	$330F	DC.L 0	 ;  GetItemMark	$340F	DC.L 0	 ;  SetMItemStyle 	$350F	DC.L 0	 ;  GetItemStyle	$360F	DC.L 0	 ;  SetMenuID	$370F	DC.L 0	 ;  SetItemID	$380F	DC.L 0	 ;  SetMenuBar	$390F	DC.L SetMItemName-1		$3A0F	******* Adding new calls for System Disk 4.1 a.k.a. 5.0 *********	DC.L GetPopUpDefProc-1	$3B0F	DC.L PopUpMenuSelect-1	$3C0F	DC.L 0	 ;  Hole	$3D0F used to be DrawPopUp call	DC.L 0	 ;  NewMenu2	$3E0F	DC.L InsertMItem2-1	 ;  InsertMItem2	$3F0F	DC.L SetMenuTitle2-1 	$400F	DC.L SetMItem2-1		$410F	DC.L SetMItemName2-1	$420F	DC.L NewMenuBar2-1		$430F	DC.L 0	 ;  GetResMTitle 	$440F	DC.L HideMenuBar-1		$450F patched 26-Aug-91 DAL	DC.L 0	 ;  ShowMenuBar	$460F*** new calls for System Disk 6.0 ***	DC.L SetItemIcon-1		$470F New calls to support	DC.L GetItemIcon-1		$480F icons in menu items.	DC.L SetItemStruct-1	$490F	DC.L GetItemStruct-1	$4A0F	DC.L RemoveItemStruct-1	$4B0F	DC.L GetItemFlag2-1		$4C0F	DC.L SetItemFlag2-1		$4D0F	DC.L GetItemWidth-1		$4E0F (Harry's call?? Added 19-Sep-90 DAL)	DC.L GetMItemBlink-1	$4F0F Added 19-Sep-90 DAL	dc.l InsertPathMItems-1	$500F Added 10-Jan-91 DALENDFPT	ENDP*****************************************************************MenuVersion	Proc** Returns the version number of the menu manager.*** Inputs:*	none** Outputs:*	version number on stack** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	lda #$0304	;2-Apr-93 DAL	sta 7,s	ENTRY QuickReturnQuickReturn	lda #0	clc	rtl	ENDP;===========================================================================;;        	MenuKey;;   IN:  Task Record, Menu Bar Handle;;  OUT:  none;; (New patch 3-Mar-91 DAL);;===========================================================================MenuKey	proc	tax	;save WAP	lda 13,s	pha	lda 13,s	pha	;pushed copy of task record	lda 13,s	pha	lda 13,s	pha	;pushed copy of Menu Bar handle	txa	;restore WAP	jsl @toROM	bcs @exit	phd	tsc	tcd@taskRec	equ 11+2	ldy #$10	;offset to TaskData field	lda [@taskRec],y	bne @claimed	ldy #$0E	;offset to modifiers	lda [@taskRec],y	and #$0100	;Apple key down?	beq @noAppleKey*** 25-Jul-91 DAL -- more restrictions on SendRequest($0F01):***   Desk Manager must be active, CDA-events must be postable (for Installer),***   and we must be dealing with the system menu bar	pha	_DeskStatus	pla	beq @notSafe	pha	pha	pea 0	pea 6	;Event Manager	_GetWAP	plx	pla	lda >$000022,x	and #$0400	;check OS Event Mask	beq @notSafe	;no CDA events allowed?*** 2-Aug-91 DAL -- our direct page isn't set!  Use X.	pha	pha	;space for GetWAP	pea 0	;system tool	pea $0F	;Menu Manager	_GetWAP	plx	pla	lda >sysmenu,x	cmp >barhand,x	bne @notSafe	lda >sysmenu+2,x	cmp >barhand+2,x	bne @notSafe*** end 2-Aug-91*** end 25-Jul-91 DAL*** since Apple was down & no item was chosen, give SendRequest($0F01) a shot at it	pea $0F01	;RequestCode for unclaimed MenuKey	pea $8000	;How=$8000: send to everyone, stop after one (26-Aug-91 DAL)	lda #0	pha	pha	;target=0 (reserved)	pei <@taskRec+2	pei <@taskRec	;data in = event pointer	pha	pha	;data out = nil	_SendRequest*** added 14-Mar-91 DAL--if a request proc takes the event, turn it into a null event	bcs @notTaken	sta [<@taskRec]	;zero it out@notTaken@notSafe*** end of 14-Mar-91 DAL@noAppleKey@claimed	pld	lda #0@exit	tax	ldy #8	jml $e10184	;ToStrip@toROM	jsl $fd6c38	;original ROM 3 MenuKey	rtl	EndP;===========================================================================;;        	GetItemBlink;;   IN:  none;;  OUT:  blink value (word).;; (New call 19-Sep-90 DAL);;===========================================================================GetMItemBlink	PROCresult	equ 7	tax	;point X at our direct page	lda >blink,x	;loads from Blink on Menu Mgr DP	sta result,s	clc	lda #0	rtl	ENDPCacheFixData	recordNumCache	ds.W 1LocalCache	ds.L 16CountTemp	ds.W 1NumInList	MenuZPage	ds.W 1	EndR ;===========================================================================;; SaveAllCache's;; This routine will save the handle to each of the menu caches that are current; this routine should be called before any routine that disposes of menu cache;; The menu mgr's direct page should be set going into this routine;;============================================================================SaveAllCache	proc	With CacheFixData		phb	phk	; change to our databank...	plb	stz NumCache	; start with no cache allocated	tdc	; save the menu mgr direct page	sta MenuZPage	ldy #2	; properly deref the menubar handle	lda [<barHand],y	sta <barPtr+2	lda [<barHand]	sta <barPtr	ROMCall getmfirst	; get the first menu handle	beq @done@loop	lda NumCache	asl a	asl a	tax	ldy #MenuFlag	; see if this menu is cached	lda [<menuptr],y	and #M_Cache	beq @notCache		ldy #MenuCache	; if it is, get the cache handle and	lda [<menuPtr],y	; save it for when the call is over	sta localCache,x	ldy #MenuCache+2	lda [<menuPtr],y	sta localCache+2,x	bra @cont@NotCache	stz localCache,x	; no cache , store zero's into our temp	stz localcache+2,x@cont		inc NumCache	; bump the menu count	ROMCall next_menu	; see if there are any more	bne @Loop	; yes, save its handle@Done	plb	; now get out...	rts	endP;===========================================================================;; DisposeCache's;; This routine will save the handle to each of the menu caches that are current; this routine should be called before any routine that disposes of menu cache;; The menu mgr's direct page should be set going into this routine;;============================================================================DisposeCache	proc	With CacheFixData; flag in <Y> says whether to purge all or not	phd	lda >MenuZPage	; switch to the menu mgr zpage	tcd	phb	phk	; change to our databank...	plb	stz CountTemp	lda NumCache	; start with no cache allocated	beq @done	; if this is zero, purge none...		sta NumInList	cpy #$FFFF	; test the input flag to see if this call	bne @notAll	; should have purged all the caches	brl @purgeAll	; if so, just do it.@notAll	ldy #2	lda [<barHand],y	sta <barPtr+2	lda [<barHand]	sta <barPtr	ROMCall getmfirst	; get the first menu handle	beq @purgeAll	; if this is zero, then purge all@loop	lda CountTemp	asl a	asl a	tax	ldy #menuCache+1	; see if the current menu is the same	lda [<menuPtr],y	; by comparing these two bytes...	cmp localCache+1,x	bne @Next	; if not the same leave us alone	dey	lda [<menuPtr],y	cmp localCache,x	bne @next	stz localCache,x	; if the same don't dispose of this one	stz LocalCache+2,x	@Next	inc CountTemp	;	dec NumCache	; bump the menu count	beq @purgeAll	; when done, exit...	ROMCall next_menu	; see if there are any more	bne @Loop	; yes, save its handle@purgeAll	stz NumCache@purgeLoop	lda NumCache	asl a	asl a	tax	lda localCache+1,x	beq @nextPurge	lda localCache+2,x	pha	lda LocalCache,x	pha	_DisposeHandle@NextPurge	lda NumCache	inc a	sta NumCache	cmp NumInList	blt @purgeLoop@Done	plb	; now get out...	pld	rts	endP;;localsetCurrentBar	PROC	lda input+2,s	Get menu bar pointer.	sta <barhand	lda input+4,s	sta <barhand+2	ora <barhand	Menu bar passed?	bne exit	ENTRY sys_currentsys_current		;       	lda <sysmenu	Caller wants the system bar.	sta <barhand	lda <sysmenu+2	sta <barhand+2	exit		rts	ENDPlocalStartup	proc	jsl IncBusyFlg	ply	phd	; save d-reg	phb	; save b-reg	pea $FDFD	; set dbr to same as in ROM	plb	plb	tcd	; set d-reg	phy	rts	endP;===========================================================================;;   MenuStartUp;; Patch to set the item blink from battery-RAM.; 17-Feb-91 DAL;===========================================================================MenuStartUp	proc	tax	lda 9,s	pha	lda 9,s	pha	txa	jsl @toROM	tax	;error code	bcs @exit	pha	pea $5E	;bram location	_ReadBParam	pla	lsr a	lsr a	lsr a	;got bits 3-4 into 0-1	and #3	pha	_SetMItemBlink	tax	;error code@exit	ldy #4	;clean up 4 bytes	jml $e10184	;ToStrip@toROM	jsl $fd5667	;ROM 3 original MenuStartUp entry	rtl	endp;===========================================================================;;   MenuShutdown;; Patch to clean up purged handles; 5/25/89 Mensch and Harry Yee;===========================================================================MenuShutdown	proc	With CacheFixDataMenuShutDownEntry	equ $FD5793MenuShutDownEntry3	equ $FD57c1	cmp #0	bne @Continue	clc	rtl@Continue	jsr localStartup	lda <sysMenu+1	beq NoBar	jsr sys_current	jsr saveAllCache	ldy #$FFFF	jsr DisposeCache	jml MenuShutDownEntryNoBar	jml MenuShutdownEntry3	endp;===========================================================================;;   MenuNewRes;; Patch to clean up purged handles; 5/25/89 Mensch and Harry Yee;===========================================================================MenuNewRes	proc	With CacheFixData	jsr localStartup	lda <sysMenu+1	beq NoBar	jsr sys_current	jsr saveAllCache	tdc	jsl MenuNewResGlue	ldy #$FFFF	jsr DisposeCacheNoBar	jml pop0BytesMenuNewResGlue	jsl ROMMenuNewRes	rtl	endp	;===========================================================================;; 	myFreeCache;;===========================================================================myFreeCache	PROC	ldy #MenuFlag	Check if there can be a cahce.	lda [<menuptr],y	and #M_CACHE	beq exit	ldy #MenuCache+1	Is there a cache?	lda [<menuptr],y	beq exit	iny	lda [<menuptr],y	pha	Put handle of cache to be disposed of on 	dey	the stack	dey	lda [<menuptr],y	pha		ldy #MenuCache+1	lda #0	Mark cache as gone.	sta [<menuptr],y	_DisposeHandle	Get rid of cacheexit	rts	ENDP;===========================================================================;; 	myEveryCacheFree;;===========================================================================myEveryCacheFree	PROC	ROMCALL getmfirst	Start with first menu.	beq exit	Are there any menus?	lop1	jsr myFreeCache	Mark cache bad if menu has a cache.	ROMCALL next_menu	Try next menu	bne lop1exit	rts	ENDP	;===========================================================================;;   DeleteMenu;; Patch to clean up purged handles; 5/25/89 Mensch and Harry Yee;===========================================================================DeleteMenu	PROC	menunum	equ input	jsr localStartup	ROMCALL lockMenuBar	beq exit2;; --- Take menu out	of menu list ---------------------------------;	lda menunum,s	ID to match.	ROMCALL getmptr	Find the menu.	beq exit	jsr myFreeCache	Release cache that may be allocated for this menu.		ldy #4	lda [<menuhand],y	and #$7FFF	Unlock the handle of menu to be removed.	sta [<menuhand],y	lop2	ROMCALL next_menu	lda <menu_cnt	sec	sbc #8	tay		lda <menuhand	sta [<barptr],y	lda <menuhand+2	iny	iny	sta [<barptr],y		ora <menuhand	Any more menu's?	bne lop2	;; --- Shrink menu record for deleted item -------------------------------------;		ldx <barhand+2	Pass menu bar's handle	lda <barhand		ldy #$FFFC	Number of bytes to decrease.	ROMCALL growBlock	Shrink the menu record.		jsr myEveryCacheFree Menus may now be in different order.	exit	ROMCALL unlockMenuBar Leave menu bar & menus unlocked.exit2	jml pop2bytes	ENDP	;===========================================================================;;   DeleteMItem;; Patch to clean up purged handles; 5/25/89 Mensch and Harry Yee;===========================================================================DeleteMItem	proc	With CacheFixData	jsr localStartup	lda <barHand+1	beq NoBar	jsr saveAllCache	tsc	tcd	pei Input	lda >MenuZPage	jsl DeleteMItemGlue	ldy #$0000	jsr DisposeCacheNoBar	jml pop2BytesDeleteMItemGlue	jsl ROMDeleteMItem	rtl	endp;===========================================================================;;   InsertMItem;; Patch to clean up purged handles; 5/25/89 Mensch and Harry Yee;===========================================================================InsertMItem	proc	With CacheFixData	jsr localStartup	lda <barHand+1	beq NoBar	jsr saveAllCache	tsc	tcd	pei Input+6	pei Input+4	pei Input+2	pei Input	lda >MenuZPage	jsl InsertMItemGlue	ldy #$0000	jsr DisposeCacheNoBar	jml pop8BytesInsertMItemGlue	jsl ROMInsertMItem	rtl	endp;===========================================================================;;   InsertMItem2;; Patch to clean up purged handles; 5/25/89 Mensch and Harry Yee;===========================================================================InsertMItem2	proc	With CacheFixData	jsr localStartup	lda <barHand+1	beq NoBar	jsr saveAllCache	tsc	tcd	pei Input+8	pei Input+6	pei Input+4	pei Input+2	pei Input	lda >MenuZPage	jsl InsertMItem2Glue	ldy #$0000	jsr DisposeCacheNoBar	jml popABytesInsertMItem2Glue	jsl ROMInsertMItem2	rtl	endp;=======================================================================;;	GetStruct;;  IN: <itemptr pts to a valid item record; OUT: <temptr contains data we're looking for;;=======================================================================GetStruct	PROC	ldy #ItemName	lda [<itemptr],y	sta <temptr	ldy #ItemName+2	lda [<itemptr],y	sta <temptr+2		ldy #ItemFlag	lda [<itemptr],y	and #$0300	Bits 8 and 9 tell us how structure is referenced.	bne @ResOrHdl	If non-zero then structure is referenced as a hdl or resource	brl doPointer@ResOrHdl	cmp #I_STRUCTisHANDLE		bne @doRes	brl doHandle@doRes	ldy #rMyItemStruct	brl doResource		;=======================================================================;; 	getrItemName; ;  IN:  <itemptr contains ptr current item record in menu ; OUT:  a = low word of ptr to item name, x = high word of ptr;;=======================================================================	ENTRY getrItemNamegetrItemName	ldy #ItemFlag	check if there is an additional structure associated with item	lda [<itemptr],y	and #I_NEWSTRUCTURE		beq OldWay	if not then field "ItemName" does indeed contain the item's name		jsr GetStruct	Get the ptr to the new structure that now contains the	ldy #ItemName2	item's name.	lda [<temptr],y	tax	ldy #ItemName2+2	lda [<temptr],y	sta <temptr+2	stx <temptr	bra GetName	We now have the reference to the item's name in <temptr.OldWay	ldy #ItemName	lda [<itemptr],y	tax	iny	iny	lda [<itemptr],y	sta <temptr+2	stx <temptrGetName	ldy #ItemFlag	lda [<itemptr],y	and #FIRST_TWO_BITS	bne @1	brl doPointer	@1	cmp #HANDLE_REF	bne @2	brl doHandle@2	ldy #rPString	;was rString 17-Sep-90 DAL	brl doResource;=======================================================================;; 	getrItemIcon; ;  IN:  <itemptr contains ptr current item record in menu ;       <temptr contains ptr to item's new structure; OUT:  a = low word of ptr to item icon, x = high word of ptr;       a & x = 0 if there is no icon associated with the icon;;=======================================================================	ENTRY getrItemIcongetrItemIcon	ldy #ItemFlag2	; Extract flag from new structure that will tell us	lda [<temptr],y	; how the icon will be referenced, i.e. ptr, hdl, resource	pha	; Save flag from structure on the stack for now.		ldy #ItemIcon	; Now extract the icon ref from this structure and put	lda [<temptr],y	; reference in <temptr.	tax	ldy #ItemIcon+2	lda [<temptr],y	sta <temptr+2	stx <temptr		pla	; check flag from struct to see how icon will be referenced	and #$0003	; Bits 8 and 9 tells us how the icon data will be referenced.	beq doPointer	; Zero means its a ptr to the icon data.@ResORHdl	cmp #$0001		beq doHandle	; Is the icon ref a handle?@IconRefIsResource	ldy #rIcondoResource	lda <temptr	; resource ID	ldx <temptr+2	ROMCALL LoadnRelease ; loads resource and releases it, then returns handle	sta <temptr	stx <temptr+2	doHandle	ldy #2	lda [<temptr],y	tax	lda [<temptr]	sta <temptr	stx <temptr+2	doPointer	lda <temptr	; low word of ptr to menu title/item name/icon ref	ldx <temptr+2	; high word of ptr to menu title/item name/icon ref		rts	ENDP	;=======================================================================;; 	getistrg;;=======================================================================getistrg	PROC	jsr getrItemName	Put item's string pointer in 'strg_ptr'	sta <strg_ptr	stx <strg_ptr+2		rts		ENDP;===========================================================================;;	GetIconInfo;;  IN: <itemptr contains ptr to current item in menu ; OUT: a-reg contains width of icon, x-reg contains height of icon;;===========================================================================getIconInfo	PROCOrigD	equ 1MyIconRect	equ OrigD+2		ldy #ItemFlag	; first check to see if there is an icon	lda [<itemptr],y	; associated with this item	and #I_NEWSTRUCTURE	beq NoIconFound		jsr GetStruct	; then check if this new structure contains	ldy #ItemFlag2	; an icon field	lda [<temptr],y	bmi GotIcon	NoIconFound	lda #0	; there's no icon so zero the appropriate output values	ldx #0	ldy #0	bra OttaHereGotIcon	jsr getrItemIcon	; get the icon's ref	phx	; put it on the stack so we can reference it easier	pha	phd	; save current direct page register	tsc 	; turn stack into direct page	tcd		ldy #oQDIconHeight		lda [<MyIconRect],y	tax	; x-reg contains the icon's height	ldy #oQDIconWidth	lda [<MyIconRect],y	; a-reg contains the icon's width	pld	; restore original direct page register	ply	; clean up stack	ply		tay	lda <ScreenMode	beq @In320Mode	tya	asl a	tay@In320Mode	tya	OttaHere	rts		ENDP;===========================================================================;; mSizeDispatch;;===========================================================================mSizeDispatch	PROC		ldy #MenuProc+1	lda [<menuptr],y	beq notCustom	brl CustomnotCustom	stz <rect+y2	Height accumulator.	stz <rect+x2	Width accumulator.; --- Set every item's height, max width, and menu's height	-----;	ROMCALL getifirst	Get pointer to first item.	beq exit	Are there any items?; ------- Find item's width --------------------;lop1	ROMCALL FixTextFace 	pha	Space for result.	jsr getistrg	Get pointer to item's string.	phx	Pass high word.	pha	Pass low word.	_StringWidth	Get string's width.	jsr GetIconInfo	a-reg contains width of icon	tax	beq @NoIcon	If a-reg is zero then there is no icon	clc	adc 1,s	Add width of item name and icon width.	adc #5	Add in some additional slop for spacing between icon.	sta 1,s	Put result back on the stack.@NoIcon		lda <text_width	Add room for the check mark.	clc		adc <text_width		adc <text_width	tax	ldy #ItemChar	lda [<itemptr],y	and #$00FF	beq ok34	lda <text_width		clc	Now add space for the keyboard equivalent, the apple key 	ror a	and a chacracter, plus one extra for slop	clc	adc <text_width	adc <text_width	1 1/2 for check mark, 2 for cmd-key-equiv,2 for space	adc <text_width		adc <text_width	adc <text_width	taxok34	txa	clc	adc 1,s	plx	Pull in x just to fix stack, a = value.; ------- Keep the width of the widest item ----------------;	cmp <rect+x2	Is this the longest	item?	bcc do_height	sta <rect+x2	Save the longest width.; ------- Accumulate item height ----------------------------;do_height	ROMCALL getitemh	Get the item's height.	clc	Keep a running height total.	adc <rect+y2	sta <rect+y2; ------- Next item	--------------------------------------------;	ROMCALL next_item	bne lop1	Any more items?	ROMCALL intoSizeMenuexit	rts	custom	ldx #mSize	ROMCALL Dispatch		rts		ENDP	;===========================================================================;;   CalcMenuSize;; Patch to clean up purged handles; 5/25/89 Mensch and Harry Yee;===========================================================================CalcMenuSize	PROCmenunum	equ inputheight	equ menunum+2theWidth	equ height+2	jsr localStartup	set DB to $FD and switch in MenuMgr d-page	ROMCALL lockMenuBar	<barptr = (<barHand), bar & menus locked	beq exit2	Is there a current menu bar?		ROMCALL to_myport	Switch to menu mgr's port		lda menunum,s	Get menu's ID.	ROMCALL getmptr	Get ptr to menu record for this ID.	beq exit	Was the menu found?		jsr myFreeCache	Free menu's cache since size maybe wrong.		ldy #MenuWidth	Set menu record with given parameters.	lda theWidth,s		bpl ok1		lda [<menuptr],y	Leave MenuWidth alone.ok1	sta [<menuptr],y	tax	iny	iny	lda height,s	bpl ok2		lda [<menuptr],y	Leave MenuHeight alone.ok2	sta [<menuptr],y	beq calc_size	Asking for default height?	txa	bne exit	Asking for default width?;; --- Compute width and height -------------------------------------------;calc_size	jsr mSizeDispatchexit	ROMCALL to_uport	Restore original port.	ROMCALL unlockMenuBar Leave menu bar & menus unlocked.exit2	jml pop6bytes	ENDP	;===========================================================================;;   SetMenuTitle;; Patch to clean up purged handles; 5/25/89 Mensch and Harry Yee;===========================================================================SetMenuTitle	proc	With CacheFixData	jsr localStartup	lda <barHand+1	beq NoBar	jsr saveAllCache	tsc	tcd	pei Input+4	pei Input+2	pei Input	lda >MenuZPage	jsl SetMenuTitleGlue	ldy #$0000	jsr DisposeCacheNoBar	jml pop6BytesSetMenuTitleGlue	jsl ROMSetMenuTitle	rtl	endp;===========================================================================;;   SetMenuTitle2;; Patch to clean up purged handles; 5/25/89 Mensch and Harry Yee;===========================================================================SetMenuTitle2	proc	With CacheFixData	jsr localStartup	lda <barHand+1	beq NoBar	jsr saveAllCache	tsc	tcd	pei Input+6	pei Input+4	pei Input+2	pei Input	lda >MenuZPage	jsl SetMenuTitle2Glue	ldy #$0000	jsr DisposeCacheNoBar	jml pop8BytesSetMenuTitle2Glue	jsl ROMSetMenuTitle2	rtl	endp;===========================================================================;;   SetMTitleWidth;; Patch to clean up purged handles; 5/25/89 Mensch and Harry Yee;===========================================================================SetMTitleWidth	proc	With CacheFixData	jsr localStartup	lda <barHand+1	beq NoBar	jsr saveAllCache	tsc	tcd	pei Input+2	pei Input	lda >MenuZPage	jsl SetMTitleWidthGlue	ldy #$0000	jsr DisposeCacheNoBar	jml pop4BytesSetMTitleWidthGlue	jsl ROMSetMTitleWidth	rtl	endp;===========================================================================;;   SetMTitleSTart;; Patch to clean up purged handles; 5/25/89 Mensch and Harry Yee;===========================================================================SetMTitleSTart	proc	With CacheFixData	jsr localStartup	lda <barHand+1	beq NoBar	jsr saveAllCache	tsc	tcd	pei Input	lda >MenuZPage	jsl SetMTitleSTartGlue	ldy #$FFFF	jsr DisposeCacheNoBar	jml pop2BytesSetMTitleSTartGlue	jsl ROMSetMTitleSTart	rtl	endp;===========================================================================;;   InsertMenu;; Patch to clean up purged handles; 5/25/89 Mensch and Harry Yee;===========================================================================InsertMenu	proc	With CacheFixData*** added 15-May-91 DAL -- make sure this isn't a duplicate menu ID	pha	phy	phd	lda 17,s	pha	lda 17,s	pha	tsc	tcd	ldy #2	lda [1],y	tax	lda [1]	sta 1	stx 3	lda [1]	;fetched menu id (first word in handle)	plx	plx	pld	;A = menu ID (first word in menu handle)	tax	beq @notDuplicate	;I'm paranoid about the zero case	pha	pha	;space for GetMHandle result	pha	;menu ID	_GetMHandle	plx	plx	beq @notDuplicate	plx	plx	;throw away saved YA	ldy #6	ldx #dupMenuID	jml $e10184	;ToStrip@notDuplicate	ply	pla*** end of 15-May-91 DAL	jsr localStartup	lda <barHand+1	beq NoBar	jsr saveAllCache	tsc	tcd	pei Input+4	pei Input+2	pei Input	lda >MenuZPage	jsl InsertMenuGlue	ldy #$0000	jsr DisposeCacheNoBar	jml pop6BytesInsertMenuGlue	jsl ROMInsertMenu	rtl	endp;===========================================================================;;   MenuSelect;; Patch to clean up purged handles; 5/25/89 Mensch and Harry Yee;;===========================================================================MenuSelect	proc	With CacheFixData	jsr localStartup;***;*** 19-Sep-90 DAL: the G_INITCURSOR bit in MenuGlobal makes MenuSelect call InitCursor;***;*** Direct page is already set to Menu Mgr direct page;***;	lda <globalFlag;	and #G_INITCURSOR;	beq @noInitCursor;	_InitCursor;@noInitCursor;*** end of 19-Sep-90 DAL addition	jsr localsetCurrentBar	jsr SaveAllCache	; this is the fix	tsc	tcd	pei Input+6	pei Input+4	pei Input+2	pei Input	lda >MenuZPage	jsl MenuSelectGlue	; now call the real menu select	bcs @error	ldy #0	jsr DisposeCache	lda #0	clc@Error	jml pop8Bytes	; now exit the call	;;;MenuSelectGlue	jsl ROMMenuSelect;;;	rtl*** added 8-Feb-92 DAL -- Patch beginning of MenuSelect to disallow pulling down***   a menu too close to the bottom of the screen.MenuSelectGlue	jsl DaveMenuSelectPatch	rtleventPtr	equ $eaDaveMenuSelectPatch	jsr localStartup	jsr localSetCurrentBar  ;<barHand = passed menu bar	ROMCALL lockMenuBar     ;<barPtr = (<barHand), bar & menus locked	beq toExitMenu2	lda $10-2,s	sta <eventPtr	lda $12-2,s	sta <eventPtr+2	;get event pointer	ldy #where	;get point of event	lda [<eventptr],y	sta <yrat	iny	iny	lda [<eventptr],y	sta <xrat	ROMCALL to_myport*** The new code -- If Top of menu bar >= 150, don't do anything, it's dangerous!	pea 0	;dummy X value	ldy #8	;offset to menu bar rect, top	lda [<barptr],y	pha	;local-coord top of menu bar	tsc	inc a	pea 0	;high word of point ptr	pha	;low word of point ptr	_LocalToGlobal	pla	;global Y value	plx	;ignore X value	cmp #150	bcs toExit*** end of the new code	jml >$fd6bdd	;back into ROM 3!toExitMenu2	jml >$fd6c2ctoExit	jml >$fd6c0a	;return menu/item = 0*** end 8-Feb-92	EndP;===========================================================================;; NewMenuBar2;; 9/07/89	Yee; When the menubar is defined as a resource, once we're done with the resource; it's not being disposed of properly. When the high word of the resource ID; is non-zero we crash.;;===========================================================================NewMenuBar2	PROC	DefineStackmenuBarPtr	longtheHandle	longorigMenuBarRef	longcount1	wordcount2	wordmem_needed	wordOrigB	byteOrigD	wordRTLAdr1	block 3RTLAdr2	block 3menuOwner	longmenuBarRef	longrefDescriptor	wordresult	longzPageSize	equ OrigB-menuBarPtr	jsl IncBusyFlg	phd	phb	pea $FDFD	plb	plb		tsc	sec 	sbc #zPageSize	tcs	tcd	;switch direct page into stack	stz <theHandle	stz <theHandle+2	stz <origMenuBarRef	stz <origMenuBarRef+2	stz <mem_needed		pha	;space for menu bar handle	pha		pei <menuOwner+2	pei <menuOwner	_NewMenuBar	;get a new menu bar		pla	;store menu bar hdl in our direct page	sta <result	pla	sta <result+2		lda <refDescriptor	asl a	tax	jmp (table,x)	table	dc.w pointer	dc.w handle	dc.w resourceIDresourceID	lda <menuBarRef	;save resource ID so we can use it to release this	sta <origMenuBarRef	;resource later	lda <menuBarRef+2	sta <origMenuBarRef+2	jml $FD5E5F	;jump back into the ROMhandle	jml $FD5E77	;jump back into the ROMpointer	jml $FD5E93	ENDP;===========================================================================;; HideMenuBar -- ROM 3 patch 26-Aug-91 DAL;; HideMenuBar in ROM is setting all SCBs to the MasterSCB, which is overkill,; and a couple developers complained.  So now it only sets the ones that; InitPalette messes with (2 through 9).;; Original function is at $FD608B in ROM 3.;;===========================================================================HideMenuBar	PROC	macro&lab	jsrlFD &addr&lab	phk	per @returnHere-1	pea $0392-1	;there is an RTL at $FD/0392 in ROM 3	jml $FD0000+&addr@returnHere	mend	jsr localStartup	lda <sysMenu+1	First check if there is a system menu bar	beq exit1	jsrlFD $6282	; sys_current; <barHand = <sysMen. Current = system	jsrlFD $628B	; lockmenubar	ldy #CtlFlag	lda [<barptr],y	tax	and #$0080	First check if menu bar is already invisible	bne ItsInvisible	txa	ora #$0080	Set invisible flag for menu bar	sta [<barptr],y	lda #1	Set Desktop operation for "toDesk", since we are hiding the	sta <temp	menu bar we need to add the rect back to the desktop.	jsrlFD $6114	; AddorSubRegion	pha	Reset all the SCBs which were initially altered	_GetMasterSCB	by InitPalette.;;;	_SetAllSCBs*** Newer way 19-Sep-91 DAL -- set SCBs 0..Height-1	ldy #$000C	;offset to bottom om menu bar rect	lda [<barPtr],y	dec a	tax	pla	;A = SCB value@setNextSCB	phx	pha	;preserve A and X	phx	pha	;push SetSCB parameters	_SetSCB	pla	plx	dex	bpl @setNextSCB*** end 19-Sep-91 DAL	jml >$fd60c0	;--> LDX <barptr+2, lda <barptrexit1	jml >$fd60d7ItsInvisible	jml >$fd60d4	EndP;===========================================================================;;   PopUpMenuSelect;;   Handle user interaction with pop-up menu. The bits M_CACHE and M_POPUP;   must be set in the menu flag. Upon entering these bits are set and;   restored to there original state when you exit.;;   IN:  PUSH:LONG - menuin: handle to menu;        PUSH:WORD - popupflag: tells us what type of popup you want;                                   $0001 = with white space;        PUSH:WORD - yloc:   top of current selection;        PUSH:WORD - xloc:   left side of "popped-up" menu;        PUSH:WORD - itemnum:item ID of current selection;;  OUT:  WORD - item selected;;===========================================================================PopUpMenuSelect	PROCmenuin	equ inputpopupflag	equ menuin+4yloc	equ popupflag+2xloc	equ yloc+2itemnum	equ xloc+2return	equ itemnum+2** New layer around PopUpMenuSelect patch, 16-Jan-91 DAL** Disable fastPort during the call, since the ROM is plastering* values back into the grafport during popPortData.*QDDirtyFlags	equ $02EC	pha	;save our WAP (low word)	pha	pha	pea 0	pea 4 	;QuickDraw	_GetWAP	plx	pla	lda >QDDirtyFlags,x	pha	phx	lda #0	sta >QDDirtyFlags,xInputParameters	equ 13	;xxx,s	ldx #7	;push 7 words for the real call@push	lda InputParameters+12,s	pha	dex	bne @push	lda 5+14,s	;get our WAP back (low word)	jsl ToOldPatch	tay	;error code	pla	sta InputParameters+12,s  ;put the result into the caller's result space	plx	pla	and #$8000	;just restore the enable/disable fastPort status (nothing cached)	sta >QDDirtyFlags,x	pla	;throw out copy of our WAP	tyx	;error code	ldy #12	jml $e10184	;ToStripToOldPatch	jsl OldPopUpMenuSelectPatch	rtlOldPopUpMenuSelectPatch	import pushPortData,popPortData	import pull_down2		jsr LocalStartup		ROMCALL lockmenubar			ROMCALL saveColor	ROMCALL GetColor		lda menuin,s	sta <menuhand	lda menuin+2,s	sta <menuhand+2		ROMCALL lockmenuhand	ROMCALL derefmenuhand	ldy #menuFlag	lda [<menuptr],y	pha	Save original menuFlag on the stack	ora #M_POPUP	Set the bit that says this is a pop-up menu	and #_M_CACHE	Clear cache bit, pop-up menus cannot be cached	sta [<menuptr],y		ROMCALL InitStuff	initialize some zero page equates		ROMCALL getifirst	get first item in menucheckNext	beq invalidItem	item not found, so return invalid item error	inc <currentSel	offset of item in list	cmp itemnum+2,s	have we found our initial selection?	beq gotit	ROMCALL next_item		bra checkNextinvalidItem	ldy #NumOfItems	make sure the menu is not empty before assigning init. sel 	lda [<menuptr],y	to first item in the menu list	bne @888	lda #1	sta <menurect+x1	dec a	sta <menurect+x2	jml popEmptyInROM@888	lda #1	If item ID is invalid then I default to the first 	sta <currentSel	item in the menu list.	gotit	jsr mSizeDispatch	get menu width and height	;=============================================================================; calculate pop-up rectangle;	lda yloc+2,s		dec a	sta <menurect+y1	top of menu	lda xloc+2,s	sta <menurect+x1	left edge of menu		ldy #menuwidth	clc	adc [<menuptr],y	sta <menurect+x2	right edge of menu		ldy #menuheight	lda [<menuptr],y	clc	adc <menurect+y1	bottom of menu	inc a	make room for drop shadow	sta <menurect+y2		lda popupflag+2,s	and #FType2PopUp	sta <saveY1		lda <currentSel	a-reg contains input to adjust rect	ROMCALL adjustRect	adjust rectangle to reflect current selection		lda <currentSel	If the current selection is the first item in list then	cmp #1	top of pop-up can't be adjusted any further.	beq noAdjustTop		ROMCALL adjustTop	current port rectangle	noAdjustTop	lda <currentSel	If the current selection is the last item in the menu then	cmp <lastVisItem	the bottom cannot be adjusted any further.	beq noAdjustBott	inc a	cmp <lastVisItem	bne @99	lda <saveY1	beq noAdjustBott	@99	ROMCALL adjustBottomnoAdjustBott		lda <portRect+x1	bne CheckLeftSideFirst		ldx <portRect+x1	lda <portRect+x2	ROMCALL justifyRight	;Move menu left if off right	ROMCALL justifyLeft		;Move menu right if off left	bra aroundCheckLeftSideFirst	ldx <portRect+x1	lda <portRect+x2	ROMCALL justifyLeft	ldx <portRect+x1	lda <portRect+x2	ROMCALL justifyRight	around		lda <saveY1	beq @222		ROMCALL doWhiteSpace  ;user wants the pop-up with the white space	@222	inc <specialFlag	;flag that tells pull_down2 to just draw box and shadow	jsr pushPortData	;save grafport vars...;; Init rect x1 and x2;	lda <menurect+x1	clc 	adc <vert_pen	sta <rect+x1	lda <menurect+x2	sec	sbc <vert_pen	dec a	subtract right drop shadow, so that drop shadow	dec a	is inside the menu rect	ldx <screenmode	beq storeit	dec a	dec astoreit	sta <rect+x2*** changed 8-Feb-92 DAL to patch out some more, down to jsr get_ids;;;	pea |RightAfterPullDown2Call-1;;;;	brl pull_down2	draw the pop-up box, drop shadow;;;;;;;;;; It never comes back, the code jumps into ROM inside pull_down2;;;	ROMCALL pull_down2	;not ROM, but it jumps there, so this works.*** copied from menumgr.asm 8-Feb-92	dec <specialFlag	;in ROM 3, this was at $FD/6988	lda <menurect+y1	inc a	pha	lda <menurect+y2	dec a	pha	lda <saveY2	bne @333	lda <menurect+y1	clc	adc <saveY1	sta <menurect+y1	bra saveWhite@333	lda <menurect+y2	sec	sbc <saveY1	sta <menurect+y2saveWhite	pla	sta <saveY2	pla	sta <saveY1	lda <menurect+x1	clc	adc <vert_pen	sta <rect+x1	lda <menurect+x2	sec	sbc <vert_pen	sta <rect+x2	ROMCALL $fd6ece	;NeverMind	bra SkipPopEmptypopEmpty	jsr PushPortDataSkipPopEmpty	ROMCALL $fd63da	;trackMenu2--track the mouse in the menu until a mouse up	jsr popPortData	;restore this grafport	lda <curselect	;get user selection and return it on the stack	beq toNoSelection*** 7-Dec-91 DAL -- call get_ids instead of loading [<itemptr] -- for custom pop-up support!;;;	lda [<itemptr]	;get the ID	ROMCALL $fd6878	;get_ids*** end 7-Dec-91toNoSelection	jml >$fd69c0	;back to noSelection in ROM 3*** end of 8-Feb-92 changes	ENDP		;------------------------------------------------------------------;;;pull_down2	PROC		stz <sav_buff+2	Set 'no cache' flag	just in case.	stz <sav_buff	ldy #MenuFlag	Check if there can be a cache.	lda [<menuptr],y	and #M_CACHE	bne cacheOK	ROMCALL allocateCache	bcc @GotCache	brl noCache@GotCache	phx	Save allocated cache.	pha	sta <sav_buff	Dereference cache.	stx <sav_buff+2	ldy #2	lda [<sav_buff],y	tay	lda [<sav_buff]	sta <sav_buff	sty <sav_buff+2	lda #0	Mark cache as BAD (not containing menu).	sta [<sav_buff]	pla	Put cache handle into sav_buff.	sta <sav_buff	pla	ora #$8000	Set temp cache flag.	sta <sav_buff+2	bra saveScreencacheOK	ldy #MenuCache+1	lda [<menuptr],y	sta <sav_buff+1	beq tryCache	Is there a cache?	dey	lda [<menuptr],y	sta <sav_buff	ldy #1	Has the cache been purged?	lda [<sav_buff],y	bne saveScreen	jsr myfreeCache	Free purged cache.tryCache	ROMCALL makeCache	Allocate a new cache for the menu.	ldy #MenuCache	lda [<menuptr],y	sta <sav_buff	iny	lda [<menuptr],y	sta <sav_buff+1;; --- Save screen to buffer ---------------------------------saveScreen	lda <sav_buff+1	beq noCache	Is there a cache?	pea 0	Pass no purge flag.***	pei <sav_buff+2	Pass cache handle.*** fixed 21-May-91 DAL -- bit 31 is a flag, so let's mask it off	lda <sav_buff+2	and #$00ff	pha	;added 22-May-91 DAL -- oops*** end of 21-May-91 DAL	pei <sav_buff	_SetPurge	Make cache nonpurgeable for now.;; Fool cache to think bottom of menuRect is 200 or less;	lda <menurect+y2	pha	cmp #200	bcc @1	lda #200@1	sta <menuRect+y2	ROMCALL cache;; Put it all back	plx	stx <menurect+y2NoCache	jml BackIntoROMSucker	EndP*@@@	if 0 then********************************************************************************PushPortData	PROC** Description:	This routine will push grafport variables that can be changed*	by menuselect and popupmenuselect. This pushes:*	BkPat*	PnLoc*	pnSize*	pnMode*	pnPat*	pnMask*	pnVis*	fontHandle*	fontID*	fontFlags*	txSize*	txFace*	txMode*	spExtra*	chExtra*	fgColor*	bgColor*** Inputs:	None** Outputs:	All that stuff on the stack!** External Refs:** Entry Points:********************************************************************************** Direct page equates for my stack frame, note that I will leave this data on the* stack and take it off with popPortData*FrameSize	equ $74	; 70 bytes of data + grafport pointerportPtr	equ 1	; the place we will use for our grafport pointerLocalPortData	equ portPtr+4	; storage area for our port pointer;; First set up our stack frame...	ply	; recover the return address and save it...	tdc	; get the current dpage	tax	; and save it in <X>	tsc	; get the stack pointer	sec	sbc #FrameSize	; adjust the stack pointer	tcs	; make it the new stack pointer and the new	tcd	; direct page	phy	; restore the return address	phx	; and save the old dpage pointer; Now get the current grafport pointer	pha	; room for result	pha	_GetPort	;	pla	sta <portPtr	; and save the port pointer to our dpage	pla	sta <portPtr+2	;; now copy $70 bytes of data to our localportdata area	ldy #$8E	; last address to copy from	ldx #$6E	; last data to copy@CopyLoop	lda [<portPtr],y	; get the byte of data	sta <LocalPortData,x ; and save it	dey	dey	dex	dex	bpl @CopyLoop; now that we are done, lets get the proper direct page off the stack and end...	pld	rts	; now leave	EndP	EJECT********************************************************************************PopPortData	PROC** Description:	This routine will pop grafport variables that can be changed*	by MenuSelect and PopUpMenuSelect.**             NOTE: You must have called PushPortData first, and the stack must*	be set to what it was when pushPortData returned.**        This pops:*	BkPat*	PnLoc*	pnSize*	pnMode*	pnPat*	pnMask*	pnVis*	fontHandle*	fontID*	fontFlags*	txSize*	txFace*	txMode*	spExtra*	chExtra*	fgColor*	bgColor*** Inputs:	None** Outputs:	All that stuff on the stack!** External Refs:** Entry Points:********************************************************************************** Direct page equates for my stack frame, note that I will leave this data on the* stack and take it off with popPortData*FrameSize	equ $74	; 70 bytes of data + grafport pointersavedDPage	equ 1Rtn1	equ savedDPage+2portPtr	equ Rtn1+2	; the place we will use for our grafport pointerLocalPortData	equ portPtr+4	; storage area for our port pointer; first copy $70 bytes of data from our localportdata area to the port	phd	; save the old dPage	tsc	; now make the stack the dPage	tcd	ldy #$8E	; last address to copy from	ldx #$6E	; last data to copy@CopyLoop	lda <LocalPortData,x ; and save it	sta [<portPtr],y	; get the byte of data	dey	dey	dex	dex	bpl @CopyLoop; Now that we are finished, reset the old dPage and pull all the old shit; off the stack*** added 16-Jan-91 DAL to make this thing work with fastPort on!*** Just set the port to what it already is to clear the fastPort*** dirty flags & make items always hilite properly. BRC:MS902MSC.	pha	pha	_GetPort	_SetPort*** end of 16-Jan-91 DAL fix	pld	; restore the directpage	ply	; save the return address for a sec...	tsc	; now adjust the stack pointer	clc	adc #FrameSize	tcs	; and resave the stack pointer	phy	; restore the return address	rts	; now leave	ENDP	endif* @@@;==========================================================================;;	GetPopUpDefProc;;         	Return the address of the pop-up definition procedure.;;   IN:    None.;;  OUT:    Address of list definition procedure.;==========================================================================GetPopUpDefProc	PROC	import PopupProcTheResult	equ 7	lda #PopupProc>>16	Pass pointer to list control defProc.	sta TheResult+2,s	lda #PopupProc	sta TheResult,s	brl QuickReturn		ENDP;===========================================================================;; 	DrawItemIcon;;  IN: <itemptr pts to item record currently being worked on;; OUT: if item has an icon associated with it then we draw it, otherwise;      we just return;;===========================================================================DrawItemIcon	PROC	jsr GetStruct	ldy #itemflag2	lda [<temptr],y	bpl @noIcon;; Setup parameters for PPToPort to draw the icon.;	jsr getrItemIcon	x = high word of ref to icon record, a = low word	phx	a & x contain pointer to icon structure.	pha			pea 0	Display mode.		lda <text_width	clc	don't wan't any carry to be rotating in on us	ror a	clc	adc <rect+x1	adc <text_width	Ident 1 1/2 times the width of 'W' to make room for mark 	pha	x coordinate of upper left corner of destination	;; Center icon in <rect;	jsr GetIconInfo	phx	get height of icon	lda <rect+y2	sec	sbc <rect+y1	calculate the height of the item's rect	sec	sbc 1,s	subtract height of icon from height of item rect	clc		ror a	take half of that to use to center icon	sta 1,s	lda <rect+y1	add this to the y1 coordinate of item rect  	clc	to get the y coordinate of the upper left corner 	adc 1,s	of the destination	sta 1,s	*** added 26-Mar-91 DAL to make the color right (stolen from MenuMgr.asm)	lda 3,s	and #$fffe	sta 3,s*** end of 26-Mar-91 DAL	_DrawIcon	bcc @noIcon	cmp #$0002	QDAux not started?	bne @noIcon		tsc	clc	Clean up stack.	adc #10	tcs@noIcon	rts		ENDP;==========================================================================;; DoADirtyDeed2;; Patches return address from SetForeColor call to return to the patch for; routine text_guts.;;==========================================================================DoADirtyDeed2	PROC EXPORTRTL1	equ 1	; stack offsets from SetForeColorMenuRTL	equ RTL1+3theForeColor	equ MenuRTL+3BackIntoTextGuts	equ $FD730C; the code leading up to this point...;; 	ldy <norcolor	Normal color.; 	tax	Is item selected?; 	beq ok1;	ldy <hiliteclr	If yes, use hilite color.; ok1	tya;	and #$000F;	jsr pushSmearLow	Push smeared color;	_SetForeColor;	lda >PatchEntry2	sta MenuRTL,s	lda >PatchEntry2+1	sta MenuRTL+1,s	brl FinishSetForeColorPatchEntry2	dc.L theDirtyDeed2theDirtyDeed2	NOP	ldy #ItemFlag	lda [<itemptr],y	and #I_NEWSTRUCTURE	bne doPatch	jml BackIntoTextGuts	doPatch	ROMCALL FixTextFace;; --- Dividing line (not the same thing as an underline) -------------;	jsr getistrg		lda [<strg_ptr] 	Get the first two bytes from the string	cmp #$2D01	Dividing line flag?	bne main_text	lda <rect+y2	Center line in item.	sec	sbc <rect+y1	lsr a	clc	adc <rect+y1	tay			lda <rect+x1	Draw from wall to wall.	ldx <rect+x2	dex	Not past right side.	ROMCALL hline	Draw the dividing line and exit.	bra ck_dim	;; --- Print item's text ----------------------------------------------;main_text		; !!!! Font not defined yet !!!!	lda <rect+y2		sec	sbc <descent	tay	Y = position to print item	phy		lda <text_width	clc	don't want any carry to be rotating in on us	ror a	clc	adc <rect+x1	adc <text_width	Indent 1 1/2 times the width of "w" to make room for mark	pha	x starting position of item's text	jsr GetIconInfo	tax	beq @noIcon	clc	adc 1,s	Add in the width of the icon.	adc #2	Add some extra slop for spacing in between the icon.	sta 1,s@noIcon	plx	ply	ROMCALL printstrg		jsr DrawItemIcon	If the itemhas an icon this routine draws it, otherwise;		it just returns	jml $FD7340	Jump back into ROM (JSR ClearTextFace)	ck_dim	jml $FD7391	Jump back to label ck_dim in ROM.	ENDP;==========================================================================;; DoADirtyDeed3;; Patches return address from PtInRect call to return to the patch for; routine choose_item. Patches call "INSIDE" which is called by Choose_Item.;;==========================================================================DoADirtyDeed3	PROC EXPORTtlRTL	equ 1MenuMgrRTL	equ tlRTL+3theRectPtr	equ MenuMgrRTL+3thePointPtr	equ theRectPtr+4theResult	equ thePointPtr+4BackIntoINSIDE	equ $FD6CD1; the code leading up to this point...;	tay;;	pha	Space for result.;;	pea 0	Pass address of point to check.;	tdc;	clc;	adc #yrat;	pha;;	phx	Pass address of RECT to check.;	phy;	_PtInRect		lda >PatchEntry3	sta MenuMgrRTL,s	lda >PatchEntry3+1	sta MenuMgrRTL+1,s	brl FinishPtInRectPatchEntry3	dc.L theDirtyDeed3theDirtyDeed3	NOP	ldy #itemflag	lda [<itemptr],y	and #I_NEWSTRUCTURE	bne @doPatch	jml BackIntoINSIDE	Right after PtInRect call.@doPatch	pla		plx	Get rts from call to INSIDE off stack	tax		bne no_Scroller	lop5	inc <count	Next item	lda <count	ROMCALL calcitem	Get item's RECT and pointer.	beq not_found	Off end of menu?		ldx #0	Check if cursor is inside item.	tdc	clc	adc #rect	ROMCALL inside	beq lop5;; --- Cursor over item --------------------------------------------;no_scroller	jsr getistrg	All this just to patch this routine.	jml $FD70A1	not_found	jml $FD70C4	ENDP		;===========================================================================;;        	SetItemIcon;; This routine sets the ItemIcon field of the item structure referenced; by the value now in the itemname field.; The ItemFlag2 field in this structure is also set according to how ; the icon will be referenced.;;   IN:  PUSH:WORD - refdescriptor for icon data;        PUSH:LONG - reference to icon data;        PUSH:WORD - item ID ;;  OUT:  None.;;===========================================================================SetItemIcon	PROCitemnum	equ inputiconRef	equ itemnum+2iconVerb	equ iconRef+4	jsr localstartup	ROMCALL lockmenubar	beq exit2	lda itemnum,s	Get item's ID.	ROMCALL getiptr	Now get its pointer.	beq exit	Error?	ldy #ItemFlag	First check if we've got our new style item record	lda [<itemptr],y	that allows icons.	and #I_NEWSTRUCTURE	beq ERROR	If zero then item record not setup properly to handle icons.		ROMCALL badCache		jsr GetStruct	Get pointer to this new structure.	ldy #ItemFlag2	lda [<temptr],y	and #$FFFC	Clear bits 0 and 1 which indicate how the icon will be	ora iconVerb,s	referenced and "OR" in new verb.	ora #I_NOICON	Set bit in flag that tells us there is an icon associated w/item.	sta [<temptr],y		ldy #ItemIcon	Store the icon ref in our structure.	lda iconRef,s	sta [<temptr],y	ldy #ItemIcon+2	lda iconRef+2,s	sta [<temptr],yexit	ROMCALL unlockmenubarexit2	jml pop8bytes	no errorERROR	ROMCALL unlockmenubar	ldy #NoStruct	error, "Invalid access of new item structure."	jml epop8bytes		ENDP;===========================================================================;;        	GetItemIcon;;   IN:  PUSH:LONG - result containing reference to item's icon;        PUSH:WORD - item ID ;;  OUT:  LONG - Reference to item's icon. Result is zero if there is no icon.;;===========================================================================GetItemIcon	PROCitemnum	equ inputresult	equ itemnum+2	jsr localstartup	ROMCALL lockmenubar	beq exit2	lda #0	Initialize result to zero.	sta result,s	sta result+2,s		lda itemnum,s	ROMCALL getiptr	beq exit	item not found		ldy #ItemFlag	Check if correct flags are set to indicate use of the 	lda [<itemptr],y	new structure.	and #I_NEWSTRUCTURE	beq ERROR	If zero item record not setup to handle icons.		jsr GetStruct	Get reference to new structure and put in <temptr.	ldy #ItemFlag2	Make sure structure is using ItemIcon field. 	lda [<temptr],y		and #I_NOICON	beq exit	If not, then we're done.		ldy #ItemIcon	 Get the reference to the icon and put in result.	lda [<temptr],y	sta result,s	ldy #ItemIcon+2	lda [<temptr],y	sta result+2,s		exit	ROMCALL unlockmenubarexit2	jml pop2bytesERROR	ROMCALL unlockmenubar	ldy #NoStruct	jml epop2bytes		ENDP	;===========================================================================;;        	SetItemStruct;;   IN:  PUSH:WORD - ItemStructVerb, describes how STRUCT will be referenced;        PUSH:LONG - ItemStructRef, ptr, hdl, resource ID to STRUCT;        PUSH:WORD - ItemID, ID of item to set;;  OUT:  None.;; This call allows a menu item specified by ItemID to now be associated with; a new structure. The ref. to this structure now resides in the ITEMNAME field; of the item's record. Bits 10, 9, and 8 are automatically set. The ref to the; item's name is then stored in this new structure.;;===========================================================================SetItemStruct	PROCitemnum	equ inputItemStructRef	equ itemnum+2ItemStructVerb	equ ItemStructRef+4	jsr localstartup		ROMCALL lockmenubar	beq exit2	If a reg is zero upon return then no menubar present.	lda itemnum,s	ROMCALL getiptr	Returns ptr to item record in <itemptr	beq exit	If a reg is zero upon return then item not found.		ROMCALL badCache		ldy #ItemFlag	Set bit 10 in itemflag to indicate that the field	lda ItemStructVerb,s itemname is now a Ref. to this new structure.	xba	Also set bits 8 and 9 to reflect how this structure	ora #I_NEWSTRUCTURE	will be referenced.	ora [<itemptr],y	sta [<itemptr],y			ldy #ItemName+2	Save ref. to item's name on stack.	lda [<itemptr],y	pha	ldy #ItemName	lda [<itemptr],y	pha		lda ItemStructRef+4,s Now store the ref. to the struct in the itemname field.	sta [<itemptr],y	lda ItemStructRef+6,s	iny	iny	sta [<itemptr],y		jsr GetStruct	Returns a ptr to the new structure in <temptr.	ldy #ItemName2	Store itemname in its new location.	pla	sta [<temptr],y	pla	iny	iny	sta [<temptr],y	exit	ROMCALL unlockmenubarexit2	jml pop8bytes	ENDP	;===========================================================================;;        	GetItemStruct;;   IN:  PUSH:LONG - Result, ref to item's struct is returned here;        PUSH:WORD - ItemID, ID of item's struct you want;;  OUT:  None.;; If bit 10 is set, then this call returns the reference to the item's ; structure.;;===========================================================================GetItemStruct	PROCitemnum	equ inputresult	equ itemnum+2	jsr localstartup	ROMCALL lockmenubar	beq exit2	If a-reg is zero upon return then no menubar present.		lda #0	Initialize result to zero for time being.	sta result,s	sta result+2,s		lda itemnum,s	ROMCALL getiptr	beq exit	If a-reg is zero upon return then item not found.		ldy #ItemFlag	See if item has additional structure associated with it.	lda [<itemptr],y	and #I_NEWSTRUCTURE	beq exit		ldy #ItemName	lda [<itemptr],y	sta result,s	iny	iny	lda [<itemptr],y	sta result+2,s	exit	ROMCALL unlockmenubarexit2	jml pop2bytes	ENDP		;===========================================================================;;        	RemoveItemStruct;;   IN:  PUSH:WORD - ItemID, ID of item's struct you want removed;;  OUT:  None.;;===========================================================================RemoveItemStruct	PROCitemnum	equ input	jsr localstartup	ROMCALL lockmenubar	beq exit2	If a-reg is zero upon return then no menubar present.		lda itemnum,s	ROMCALL getiptr	beq exit	If a-reg is zero upon return then item not found.		ldy #ItemFlag	lda [<itemptr],y	and #I_NEWSTRUCTURE	First check to make sure there is a structure.	beq exit		ROMCALL badCache		jsr GetStruct	Move itemname ref from the structure back to the	ldy #ItemName2+2	item's record.	lda [<temptr],y	tax	ldy #ItemName2	lda [<temptr],y	ldy #ItemName	sta [<itemptr],y	iny	iny	txa	sta [<itemptr],y		ldy #ItemFlag	lda [<itemptr],y	and #$F8FF	Clear bits 10, 9, and 8.	sta [<itemptr],y	exit	ROMCALL unlockmenubarexit2	jml pop2bytes		ENDP	;===========================================================================;;        	GetItemFlag2;;   IN:  PUSH:WORD - Result;        PUSH:WORD - ItemID, ID of item that you want flag for.;;  OUT:  None.;;===========================================================================GetItemFlag2	PROCitemnum	equ inputresult	equ itemnum+2	jsr localstartup	ROMCALL lockmenubar	beq exit2	If a-reg is zero upon return then no menubar present.		lda #0	sta result,s		lda itemnum,s	ROMCALL getiptr	beq exit	If a-reg is zero upon return then item not found.		ldy #ItemFlag	lda [<itemptr],y	and #I_NEWSTRUCTURE	beq exit		jsr GetStruct	ldy #ItemFlag2	lda [<temptr],y	sta result,sexit	ROMCALL unlockmenubarexit2	jml pop2bytes		ENDP		;===========================================================================;;        	SetItemFlag2;;   IN:  PUSH:WORD - ItemFlag2, new value you want ItemFlag2 to be set to;        PUSH:WORD - ItemID, ID of item that you want to set.;;  OUT:  None.;;===========================================================================SetItemFlag2	PROCitemnum	equ inputNewItemFlag2	equ ItemNum+2	jsr localstartup	ROMCALL lockmenubar	beq exit2	If a-reg is zero upon return then no menubar present.		lda itemnum,s	ROMCALL getiptr	beq exit	If a-reg is zero upon return then item not found.		ldy #ItemFlag	lda [<itemptr],y	and #I_NEWSTRUCTURE	beq exit		ROMCALL badCache		jsr GetStruct	ldy #ItemFlag2	lda NewItemFlag2,s	sta [<temptr],yexit	ROMCALL unlockmenubarexit2	jml pop4bytes		ENDP;===========================================================================;;        	GetItemWidth;;   IN:  PUSH:WORD - ItemFlag2, new value you want ItemFlag2 to be set to;        PUSH:WORD - ItemID, ID of item that you want to set.;;  OUT:  None.;;; 21-Sep-90 Dave Lyons;; Harry added this to the Menu Manager tool, but not to the ROM 3 patch,; so here's where it will be.;;===========================================================================GetItemWidth	proc	brk 0		;%%%		EndP;===========================================================================;;	SetMItem;;        	Set new item string.;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - pointer to new string.;          PUSH:WORD - item's ID.;;  OUT:    None.;;===========================================================================SetMItem	PROCitemnum	equ inputstrg	equ itemnum+2BackIntoSetMItem	equ $FD7A9A	Back into SetMItem call in ROM.	jsr localstartup	ROMCALL lockmenubar	<barptr = (<barHand), bar & menus locked.	beq exit2		lda itemnum,s	Get pointer to item's record and store in <itemptr.	ROMCALL getiptr	beq exit		ldy #itemflag	Check if item has new structure associated with it.	lda [<itemptr],y	and #I_NEWSTRUCTURE	bne @newWay		jml BackIntoSetMItem@newWay	ROMCALL badCache	Set cache to bad if	menu has a cache.	ldy #ItemFlag	Since the reference to the item name is a ptr to that name	lda [<itemptr],y	we clear the first two bits of the item flag	and #CLEAR_TWO_BITS	sta [<itemptr],y		lda strg,s	Pass pointer to string.	sta <strg_ptr	lda strg+2,s	sta <strg_ptr+2	ROMCALL parse_strg	Get and set length of string.		jsr GetStruct	Get ptr to item's additional structure.	ldy #itemName2	lda <strg_ptr	sta [<temptr],y	lda <strg_ptr+2	iny	iny	sta [<temptr],y	exit	ROMCALL unlockmenubar Leave menu bar & menus unlocked.exit2	jml pop6bytes		ENDP;===========================================================================;;	GetItem;;        	Get item's string.;;   IN:  PUSH:WORD - item's ID.;;  OUT:  LONG - pointer to item's text.;;===========================================================================GetItem	PROCitemnum	equ inputresult	equ itemnum+2BackIntoGetItem1	equ $FD7AD3	Back into GetItem if item not found.BackIntoGetItem2	equ $FD7ADC	Back into GetItem if item doesn't have new struct associated with it.	jsr localstartup	ROMCALL lockmenubar	<barptr = (<barHand), bar & menus locked.	beq exit2		lda itemnum,s	Get pointer to item's record and store in <itemptr.	ROMCALL getiptr	bne foundSomething	jml BackIntoGetItem1	foundSomething	ldy #ItemFlag	First check is there is the new structure associated	lda [<itemptr],y	with this item.	and #I_NEWSTRUCTURE	bne @newWay	jml BackIntoGetItem2@newWay	jsr GetStruct	Get ptr to item's additional structure.	ldy #itemName2	lda [<temptr],y	sta result,s	iny	iny	lda [<temptr],y	sta result+2,s		ROMCALL unlockmenubarexit2	jml pop2bytes	ENDP;===========================================================================;; EnableMItem patch;; 22-Oct-90 Dave Lyons;; Return an error if the Menu Manager isn't started up, because some; stupid application is calling this before it starts any tools.;;===========================================================================EnableMItem	proc	tay	beq ReturnError0001	jml >$fd7b62		entry ReturnError0001ReturnError0001	lda #1	sec	rtl	endp;===========================================================================;; DisableMItem patch;; 22-Oct-90 Dave Lyons;; Return an error if the Menu Manager isn't started up, because some; stupid application is calling this before it starts any tools.;;===========================================================================DisableMItem	proc	import ReturnERror0001	tay	beq ReturnError0001	jml >$fd7b76	endp;===========================================================================;;	SetMItemName;;        	Set item's string.;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - pointer to pascal string.;          PUSH:WORD - item's ID.;;  OUT:    None.;;===========================================================================SetMItemName	PROCitemnum	equ inputnewName	equ itemnum+2BackToSetMItemName	equ $FD7B42	jsr localstartup	Do startup initialization for tool call.	ROMCALL lockMenuBar	<barPtr = (<barHand), bar & menus locked.	beq exit2	Is there a current menu bar?	lda itemnum,s	Get item's ID.	ROMCALL getiptr	Now get its pointer.	beq exit	Error?	ldy #ItemFlag	First check if item has new structure associated with it.	lda [<itemptr],y	and #I_NEWSTRUCTURE	bne @newWay		jml BackToSetMItemName@newWay	ROMCALL badCache	Set cache to bad if	menu has a cache.	ldy #ItemFlag	Get flag of current item and clear the first two bits	lda [<itemptr],y	We need to clear them because later on we're going to	and #CLEAR_TWO_BITS 'OR' it with the new value	sta [<itemptr],y		jsr GetStruct	Get the ptr to the new structure	ldy #itemName2	and store the ptr in <temptr.	lda newName,s	sta [<temptr],y	iny	iny	lda newName+2,s	sta [<temptr],yexit	ROMCALL unlockMenuBar Leave menu bar & menus unlocked.exit2	jml pop6bytes	no error	ENDP	;===========================================================================;;	SetMItemName2;;  IN: PUSH:WORD - refdescriptor, describes what next long will be;      PUSH:LONG - titleref, pointer, handle, or resource ID of title name;      PUSH:WORD - menuitem, ID of item that will get new title;; OUT: None.;;===========================================================================SetMItemName2	PROCitemnum	equ inputtitleref	equ itemnum+2	; ptr, hdl, resource ID of new item namerefdescriptor	equ titleref+4BackToSetMItemName2	equ $FD7AFEBackIntoCall	equ $FD7B0E	jsr localstartup	ROMCALL lockMenuBar	beq exit2	lda itemnum,s	Get item's ID.	ROMCALL getiptr	Now get its pointer (in <itemptr).	beq exit	Error?		ldy #ItemFlag	lda [<itemptr],y	and #I_NEWSTRUCTURE	bne @newWay		jml BackToSetMItemName2@newWay	ROMCALL badCache	Set cache to bad if	menu has a cache.	jsr GetStruct	There is so get the ptr to the new structure	ldy #itemName2	and store the ptr in <temptr.	lda titleref,s	sta [<temptr],y	iny	iny	lda titleref+2,s	sta [<temptr],y	jml BackIntoCallexit	ROMCALL unlockMenuBar		exit2	jml pop8bytes		ENDP;===========================================================================;;	SetMItem2;;  IN: PUSH:WORD - refdescriptor, describes what next long is (0=ptr, 1=hdl, 2=res ID);      PUSH:LONG - titleref, pointer, handle or resource ID of a resource menu item;      PUSH:WORD - item's ID;; OUT: None.;;===========================================================================SetMItem2	PROCitemnum	equ inputtitleref	equ itemnum+2	; ptr, hdl, resource ID of new item namerefdescriptor	equ titleref+4myTemp	equ worknewFlag	equ myTemp+4BackInSetMItem2	equ $FD7A21	jsr localstartup	ROMCALL lockmenubar	bne @FoundMenuBar	brl exit2	@FoundMenuBar	lda itemnum,s	Is the item that we specified in any of the menus?	ROMCALL getiptr	Put the ptr to the item record in <itemptr.	bne @FoundItem	brl exit	Item not found so just beat it.@FoundItem		ldy #ItemFlag 	First check if the new structure is associated with this item.	lda [<itemptr],y	and #I_NEWSTRUCTURE	bne @newWay		jml BackInSetMItem2 Nothing new so just run the old code.@newWay		ROMCALL badCache	Set cache to bad if menu has a cache		ldy #ItemFlag	Get flag of current item and clear the first two bits	lda [<itemptr],y	We need to clear them because latter on we're going to	and #CLEAR_TWO_BITS 'OR' it with the new value	sta [<itemptr],y		lda titleref,s		sta <myTemp	lda titleref+2,s	sta <myTemp+2			lda refdescriptor,s		asl a	tax	jmp (table,x)	table	dc.w pointer	dc.w handle	dc.w resourceID	resourceID	lda titleref+2,s	Load the menu item resource and get the handle to it	tax		lda titleref,s	ldy #rMenuItem	ROMCALL LoadnRelease	sta <myTemp	Store handle back on my direct page	stx <myTemp+2	handle	ldy #2	Dereference the menu item handle and put ptr back	lda [<myTemp],y	into my direct page	tax	lda [<myTemp]	sta <myTemp	stx <myTemp+2	pointer	ldy #resItemFlag	Find out how the item name is being referenced, is it a	lda [<myTemp],y	pointer, handle, or resource ID?	and #FIRST_TWO_BITS	sta <newFlag		ldy #ItemFlag	lda [<itemptr],y	ora <newFlag	sta [<itemptr],y	Update the item flag in our item record		jsr GetStruct	Get the ptr to the new structure and store the ptr in <temptr.	ldy #resItemName	Store new itemname in new structure.	lda [<myTemp],y		ldy #ItemName2	sta [<temptr],y	ldy #resItemName+2	lda [<myTemp],y	ldy #ItemName+2	sta [<temptr],yexit	ROMCALL unlockmenubarexit2	jml pop8bytes	ENDP			END		